    {
      "file": "src/lib/libdwarf/dwarf_elf_load_headers.c",
      "function": "read_gs_section_group",
      "line": null,
      "code": "if (gseca > ep->f_loc_shdr.g_count) {\n    /*  Might be confused endianness by\n        the compiler generating the SHT_GROUP.\n        This is pretty horrible. */\n\n    if (gsecb > ep->f_loc_shdr.g_count) {\n        *errcode = DW_DLE_ELF_SECTION_GROUP_ERROR;\n        free(data);\n        free(grouparray);\n        return DW_DLV_ERROR;\n    }\n    /* Ok. Yes, ugly. */\n    gseca = gsecb;\n    grouparray[i] = gseca;\n}",
      "note": "The staged patch changes both section-number comparisons here from `>` to `>=`. On the witnessed bytes `04 00 00 00`, the primary decode already yields `gseca == 4`, so the `gsecb` fallback is not needed; the bug is that the equality case is treated as in range.",
      "kind": "root_cause_function"
    },
